        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "glossary",
          "nodeId": "glossary-reading"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#222b49,#171f38);border:2px solid #b8d8ff88;border-radius:18px;padding:5cqw;color:#f8f3ff;font-family:system-ui'><div style='color:#b8d8ff;font:800 3.4cqw system-ui;letter-spacing:.16em'>01 / READING</div><h2 style='margin:3cqw 0 2cqw;font:600 8cqw/.98 Georgia,serif'>A visitor&#39;s vocabulary</h2><p style='margin:0 0 3cqw;font:400 3.2cqw/1.42 system-ui;color:#bfcce7'>What you need to understand what you see.</p><div style='border-top:1px solid #48516b;padding:2cqw 0'><b style='display:block;color:#b8d8ff;font:700 3.9cqw/1.2 system-ui'><strong>graph</strong></b><span style='font:400 3.0cqw/1.42 system-ui;color:#d0d8e9'>A thing you can open: a set of nodes and the edges between them, saved as one <code style='color:#e6c987;background:#242c48;border-radius:4px;padding:0 3px'>.node</code> file with its own address (<code style='color:#e6c987;background:#242c48;border-radius:4px;padding:0 3px'>tlz://host/path/root.node</code>).</span></div><div style='border-top:1px solid #48516b;padding:2cqw 0'><b style='display:block;color:#b8d8ff;font:700 3.9cqw/1.2 system-ui'><strong>node</strong></b><span style='font:400 3.0cqw/1.42 system-ui;color:#d0d8e9'>One thing inside a graph. Stored as an entry in <code style='color:#e6c987;background:#242c48;border-radius:4px;padding:0 3px'>nodes</code>.</span></div><div style='border-top:1px solid #48516b;padding:2cqw 0'><b style='display:block;color:#b8d8ff;font:700 3.9cqw/1.2 system-ui'><strong>edge</strong></b><span style='font:400 3.0cqw/1.42 system-ui;color:#d0d8e9'>A named connection between two nodes. Its name says what the connection means; click the name to read about that kind of connection. Stored as an entry in <code style='color:#e6c987;background:#242c48;border-radius:4px;padding:0 3px'>edges</code>.</span></div><div style='border-top:1px solid #48516b;padding:2cqw 0'><b style='display:block;color:#b8d8ff;font:700 3.9cqw/1.2 system-ui'><strong>page</strong></b><span style='font:400 3.0cqw/1.42 system-ui;color:#d0d8e9'>What a graph or a node looks like when you are close enough to read it: its first, largest face.</span></div><div style='border-top:1px solid #48516b;padding:2cqw 0'><b style='display:block;color:#b8d8ff;font:700 3.9cqw/1.2 system-ui'><strong>Portal</strong></b><span style='font:400 3.0cqw/1.42 system-ui;color:#d0d8e9'>A door to another graph. Click it to go through. Node type <code style='color:#e6c987;background:#242c48;border-radius:4px;padding:0 3px'>portal</code>.</span></div></div>"
        },
        "sourceMarkdown": "These are the only words a visitor needs to read anything in the Twilite Zone.\n\n**Graph or node.** The same thing is a graph or a node depending on where you stand. Inside it, it is a graph, with nodes of its own. From outside, it is a node: it has faces and a Glyph, and it sits in the workspace or behind a Portal like any other node. Use whichever word fits where the reader is standing.\n\n- **graph** — A thing you can open: a set of nodes and the edges between them, saved as one `.node` file with its own address (`tlz://host/path/root.node`).\n- **node** — One thing inside a graph. Stored as an entry in `nodes`.\n- **edge** — A named connection between two nodes. Its name says what the connection means; click the name to read about that kind of connection. Stored as an entry in `edges`.\n- **page** — What a graph or a node looks like when you are close enough to read it: its first, largest face.\n- **Portal** — A door to another graph. Click it to go through. Node type `portal`.",
        "memo": "Section of the Glossary. The Detail page contains the complete definitions; update both views when editing.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1794700183471,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
